<h2>AI Overview Optimization Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Definition blocks:</strong> Every strategy opens with a 1–2 sentence definition ("Strategy X is...")</li>
<li><strong>Bullet summaries:</strong> Each strategy includes a summary table with Best Season, Expected Lead Volume, and Cost</li>
<li><strong>Step-by-step instructions:</strong> Implementation sections use numbered lists where applicable</li>
<li><strong>Comparison tables:</strong> Channel CPL comparison and seasonal strategy overview tables</li>
<li><strong>FAQ schema:</strong> 12 questions with concise 60–100 word answers</li>
<li><strong>Key takeaways:</strong> Conclusion includes bullet summary of main points</li>
</ul>
<h2>GEO Optimization Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Entity-rich writing:</strong> Named companies (Kodescape, 12 Stones Roofing, Cathedral Roofing), tools (JobNimbus, AccuLynx, Hail Trace), and organizations (GAF, Owens Corning, BBB)</li>
<li><strong>Fact-based content:</strong> 40+ statistics with source attribution</li>
<li><strong>Structured answers:</strong> Every major section answers What, Why, How, When, Who</li>
<li><strong>Citations:</strong> External source suggestions for verifiable claims</li>
<li><strong>Clear definitions:</strong> Key terms defined on first use (CPL, ACV, RCV, GBP)</li>
<li><strong>Framework naming:</strong> Seasonal organization creates a memorable, citable structure</li>
</ul>
